  "notes": "{就|つ}く means to take up a position, role, or state. Written with the kanji {就|つ} to distinguish it from other つく verbs.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\nIntransitive ({自動詞|じどうし}). Always takes the particle に.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {職|しょく}に{就|つ}く: to get a job, to take employment\n- {席|せき}に{就|つ}く: to take one's seat\n- {任|にん}に{就|つ}く: to assume a post/duty\n- {床|とこ}に{就|つ}く: to go to bed (formal/literary)\n- {位|くらい}に{就|つ}く: to ascend to the throne\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{就|つ}いている means \"is in (a position)\" — resulting state.\n\nCOMPOUNDS:\n- {就職|しゅうしょく}する: to get employed\n- {就任|しゅうにん}する: to take office\n- {就寝|しゅうしん}する: to go to bed (formal)",
